{
  "$comment": "Routes of the engine's HTTP API (plan §13, §25). One route per EngineAPI method (operation), plus the server's own (login, logout, page, assets, diagnosticsDownload). Request and response bodies are $defs of api/dtos.json. Each platform's Router table is generated from this file, and the API contract tests check every route of every platform's Server against it.",
  "conventions": [
    "Bodies are JSON (application/json; charset=utf-8). Errors are ErrorBody with the status given for the code in shared/messages/codes.json; 401/403/404/405 come from the server.* codes.",
    "Auth: over the Unix socket every route is allowed (peer credentials). Over TCP: 'read' routes need a read or control token (Bearer, or the login cookie); 'control' routes need a control token; 'none' routes need nothing. Every POST, PUT, PATCH and DELETE also needs the header X-Bromelia: 1 and, when the request has an Origin, one the server serves. Without any token configured, only Host localhost, 127.0.0.1 and [::1] (and server.allowedHosts) are served. No token is ever taken from the URL.",
    "Path parameters: {driveId} DriveId, {sessionId} {jobId} {unitId} Uuid, {libraryId} {stepId} {targetId} EntryId, {name} a secret name or a file name.",
    "Lists are paged with ?cursor= and ?limit=; the response's next is the cursor of the following page.",
    "PUT /v1/config and PATCH /v1/sessions/{id} are optimistic: they carry the version / rev they were based on and get 409 when it is stale."
  ],
  "routes": [
    {
      "operation": "system",
      "method": "GET",
      "path": "/v1/system",
      "auth": "read",
      "response": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": "SystemStatus"
      }
    },
    {
      "operation": "stop",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/v1/system/stop",
      "auth": "control",
      "response": {
        "status": 202
      },
      "errors": [
        "server.stopping"
      ],
      "note": "Asks the engine to stop: acquisitions are cancelled, then jobs settle (plan §15.1). The app's 'Quit Bromelia completely'."
    },
    {
      "operation": "drives",
      "method": "GET",
      "path": "/v1/drives",
      "auth": "read",
      "response": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": "Drives"
      }
    },
    {
      "operation": "eject",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/v1/drives/{driveId}/eject",
      "auth": "control",
      "response": {
        "status": 204
      },
      "errors": [
        "drive.notFound",
        "drive.busy",
        "drive.ejectFailed"
      ]
    },
    {
      "operation": "closeTray",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/v1/drives/{driveId}/close-tray",
      "auth": "control",
      "response": {
        "status": 204
      },
      "errors": [
        "drive.notFound",
        "drive.closeTrayFailed"
      ]
    },
    {
      "operation": "closeAllTrays",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/v1/drives/close-trays",
      "auth": "control",
      "response": {
        "status": 204
      },
      "errors": [
        "drive.closeTraysFailed"
      ]
    },
    {
      "operation": "rip",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/v1/drives/{driveId}/rip",
      "auth": "control",
      "request": "RipOptions",
      "response": {
        "status": 201,
        "body": "Job"
      },
      "errors": [
        "drive.notFound",
        "drive.noDisc",
        "drive.busy",
        "disc.notVideo",
        "session.notOpen",
        "session.noTitlesChosen",
        "session.nothingToRip",
        "library.offline",
        "library.none",
        "makemkv.notFound"
      ],
      "note": "Rip with the drive's profile and title rules; with options.titles, those titles of the open session as MKV files."
    },
    {
      "operation": "cancelCountdown",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/v1/drives/{driveId}/cancel-countdown",
      "auth": "control",
      "response": {
        "status": 204
      },
      "errors": [
        "drive.notFound"
      ],
      "note": "Stops an automatic rip's countdown. Not in plan §13.1's list: AutomationService.cancelCountdown (§11.1) needs a route, and today's apps offer it (cancelling a waiting automatic job)."
    },
    {
      "operation": "openSession",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/v1/sessions",
      "auth": "control",
      "request": "SessionSource",
      "response": {
        "status": 201,
        "body": "Session"
